		<!-- Content -->
		<div class="container"><h1>Quickstart</h1>
<p>Follow these steps to download ReceiptReady and open it on your computer for the first time.</p>

<h3>What you need</h3>
<ul>
	<li>Java Development Kit (JDK) 17</li>
	<li>Apache Maven 3.8 or newer</li>
	<li>Git</li>
</ul>

<h3>Steps</h3>
<ol>
	<li>Open a terminal and download the project: <code>git clone https://github.com/bbawak1/ReceiptReady.git</code></li>
	<li>Go into the code folder: <code>cd ReceiptReady/code</code></li>
	<li>Start the app: <code>mvn javafx:run</code></li>
	<li>The first run downloads the libraries ReceiptReady needs, so it can take a minute or two.</li>
	<li>The <strong>ReceiptReady - Receipt List</strong> window opens. It is empty and shows the message "No receipts yet. Click Add to record a purchase."</li>
</ol>

<img src="/images/launch.png" width="100%" alt="ReceiptReady receipt list window after launch">

<p>You are ready to go. Next, learn how to <a href="/add">add your first receipt</a>.</p>
